# Line endings are a correctness property in this repository, not a style preference.
#
# Two things here are byte-exact by requirement:
#   * Prompt assembly has a byte-exact golden test (TASK-033, spec Section 21.9). The
#     separator is literally "\n\n", and RR-006 requires the skill body to be appended
#     verbatim, unmodified.
#   * Analyzer output must be byte-stable across runs AND across platforms (FR-011,
#     spec Section 13.3).
#
# With core.autocrlf enabled, a Windows checkout would rewrite LF to CRLF and the golden
# tests would pass locally and fail in Linux CI, or worse, the reverse. Normalize
# everything to LF in the repository, and exempt the golden fixtures from conversion
# entirely so nothing can touch them.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden and corpus fixtures: treated as binary so no filter, ever.
tests/fixtures/golden/** -text
tests/fixtures/trajectories/** -text
tests/fixtures/skills/** -text
tests/fixtures/pii/** -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not execute on Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Lockfile: hash-verified, never rewritten.
uv.lock -text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx binary
